in @prism
in @meta
in @nl
in @glass

# @code — the universal grammar-at-an-altitude discipline.
#
# The recognition (2026-06-06, Reed + Alex → Mara): mirror is one
# instance of @code (mirror as code at the mirror altitude). Rust is
# another (already declared at shards/code/rust.mirror, the D2 commit).
# LLVM, Fortran, Gleam are others (current or future). @code is the
# parent prism that names the shared discipline: "this is a grammar
# producing artifacts at altitude X."
#
# Same substrate-pull pattern as splinter_graph → mosaic(@store) and
# fragment → splinter: the word already lived in the substrate; we just
# hadn't named the inheritance. Each `@code/X` instance specializes the
# five operations at its altitude; `@code` itself declares only the
# universal five-op shape — the discipline, not the implementation.
#
# === why pure five-op (not parse / resolve / emit) ===
#
# The substrate-pull discipline (per
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]) declares parent prisms
# in their five-operation form and lets instances specialize via their
# own grammar. Pre-committing @code to a `parse(source) -> ast` /
# `resolve(ast) -> resolved` / `emit(resolved, altitude) -> au` shape
# would prematurely fix the parser-emitter pipeline as universal. But
# the existing instances (@code/rust declaring a cargo emit sub-prism;
# @code/llvm splitting into /ir and /emit) already specialize past that
# shape. The universal carrier is the five operations; the
# parse/resolve/emit shape is one common consequence at altitudes that
# have a textual surface — not a substrate-floor obligation.
#
# === sub-prism precedent ===
#
# @code/rust (shards/code/rust.mirror, D2) IS the precedent: it declares
# the five-op block at the altitude, then adds altitude-specific shape
# (the @code/rust/cargo sub-prism for emit-target identity, the
# build-property surface for settle_on). @code/mirror, @code/gleam,
# @code/llvm, @code/fortran each declare the same five-op block at their
# altitude and specialize from there.
#
# === inheritance shape: explicit `in @code` ===
#
# Each `@code/X` instance declares `in @code` at the top of its file
# (cf. boot/04a-code-rust.mirror, boot/04b-code-gleam.mirror; the
# convention preserved in the migration). The substrate uses `in @X`
# as the canonical import-and-inherit form (cf. `in @prism`,
# `in @glass`, `in @nl`). Implicit-by-namespace-nesting would
# under-declare the relationship — `@code/X` IS-A `@code` is a
# substrate fact, not a path-namespace coincidence; declaring it
# matches how every other root prism is consumed.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/spectral-triple-binary.md §3
# (translate-template altitudes); roadmap/wip/butterfly-self-hosting.md
# (the @code/llvm → @code/fortran → @code/mirror path).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]].
# Related shards: code/rust.mirror (D2; the precedent instance),
#                 code/mirror.mirror (mirror's own @code instance),
#                 code/gleam.mirror (post-migration from boot/04b).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/code.mirror` declares
# `@code` as the universal root; instances live at
# `shards/code/<name>.mirror`.

prism @code {
  focus code
  project code
  split code
  shift code
  settle code
}

out @code
